Adapted material currently covers:
- Material 3 color tokens based on Aniyomi's TachiyomiColorScheme.
- `shared/i18n` and `shared/i18n-aniyomi`: string/plural resources copied from
  Aniyomi's `i18n` and `i18n-aniyomi` modules (English base + zh-CN locale).
- `shared/presentation-core`: components, i18n helpers, screens, theme, and util
  classes ported from Aniyomi's `presentation-core` module, with small
  multiplatform substitutions (IME visibility, system-gesture exclusion,
  scrollbar metrics, preview annotations, back handling).
- `shared/presentation`: the `eu.kanade.presentation` layer copied from
  Aniyomi — library (toolbar, tabs, pager, compact/comfortable grids, list,
  settings dialog), entries (manga screen, info header, chapter list items),
  reader chrome (app bars, chapter navigator, page/settings dialogs) and
  shared components. Upstream package names and file layout are preserved so
  the module stays diffable against Aniyomi.
- `shared/domain`: preference API (interfaces and helpers) copied from
  Aniyomi's `core/common` preference package, plus a new file-backed store;
  manga/chapter/category domain models and the library/anime sort models.
- App shell (`shared/ui` home tabs, detail/reader entry screens) structured
  after Aniyomi's `ui/home` and `ui/entries` navigation code, with the
  reader's screen-model state adapted to Miyomu's `ComicReaderController`.

Android-only dependencies (Injekt DI, Context-based helpers, Android View
viewer core, SQLDelight data layer, Material motion, drawable resources) are
replaced by multiplatform equivalents; see
docs/adr/0011-kmp-aniyomi-port.md for the full substitution map.

